          %title Dual gebras
          %h1#dual_gebras Dual gebras
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#what_is_this_entry_about"} What is this entry about
              %li
                %a{:href => "#algebraic_dual"} Algebraic dual
              %li
                %a{:href => "#finite_dual"} Finite dual
              %li
                %a{:href => "#actions_on_duals"} Actions on duals
              %li
                %a{:href => "#paired_bialgebras"} Paired bialgebras
              %li
                %a{:href => "#dual_rings_of_corings"} Dual rings of corings
              %li
                %a{:href => "#literature"} Literature
          %h2#what_is_this_entry_about What is this entry about
          %p
            Following Serre,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gebra"} gebra
            is a common term for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra"} coalgebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bialgebra"} bialgebra
          %p When working over a field, finite dimensional algebras are duals to finite dimensional cogebras. When the dimension is infinite, even for algebraic duals, the situation is more complicated. This entry should eventually sort out these issues (for now only the simplest cases are discussed).
          %h2#algebraic_dual Algebraic dual
          %p
            For a commutative ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-coalgebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\Delta)
            and an associative
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,m)
            the
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_k(C,A)
            is equipped with an associative
            %strong convolution product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\star g)(c) = m(f\otimes g)(\Delta(c))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            a field, the algebraic dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*:= Hom_k(C,k)
            of a
            = succeed "-coalgebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an associative algebra, called its
            %strong dual coalgebra
            whose product is also often referred to as convolution. Correspondence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\mapsto C^*
            extends to a contravariant functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cog
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cog_k\to Alg_k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:C\to D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:D^*\to C^*
            is simply the transpose, hence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(d^*)(c) = d^*(f(c))
          %p
            Now for a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,m)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
            is
            %em not
            necessarily a coalgebra; namely the natural candidate for the comultiplication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            is the transpose operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m^*: A^*\to (A\otimes A)^*
            of the multiplication
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m: A\otimes A\to A
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*\otimes A^*\to (A\otimes A)^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            it is an isomorphism (hence taken as an identification) iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is finite dimensional over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is filtered with filtered pieces finite-dimensional), one can replace the tensor product with some completed tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat\otimes
            and define a topological comultiplication
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi m
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m^*:A^*\to A^*\hat\otimes A^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\circ
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi m
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m^*
            factors through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\circ\otimes A^\circ
          %h2#finite_dual Finite dual
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is a field, the finite dual functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Cog
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()^\circ:Alg_k\to Cog_k
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint+functor"} left adjoint functor
            to the algebraic dual as a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Cog
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()^*:Cog_k\to Alg_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\circ\subset A^*=Hom_k(A,k)
            as a vector spaces (actually as functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Vec
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_k\to Vec_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()^\circ
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfunctor"} subfunctor
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Vec
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ()^*:Alg_k\to Vec_k
          %p
            We say that a subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            of a vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is of finite codimension if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V/W
            is of finite dimension. As a vector subspace of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mtext contains an ideal of finite codimension in
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A^\circ = \{ f\in A^* \, | \, Ker(f)\, \text{contains an ideal of finite codimension in}\, A\}
          %p There are several other characterizations of the finite dual. Alternative terminologies are restricted dual and Hopf dual.
          %h2#actions_on_duals Actions on duals
          %p
            We define here left actions ⇀ (or in LaTeX
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightharpoonup
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightharpoondown
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↽
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leftharpoondown
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leftharpoonup
          %p
            (Montgomery 1.6.5) If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a coalgebra, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            the dual algebra, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            acts from the left on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by the transpose to the left multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mi ↼
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi f
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle g, c &amp;#8636; f\rangle = \langle f g, c\rangle
          %p or equivalently by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mi ↼
                  %mi c
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f &amp;#8636; c \coloneqq \langle f, c_{(1)}\rangle c_{(2)},
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+notation"} Sweedler notation
            has been used.
          %p Similarly for the right-hand action:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mi ⇀
                  %mi c
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f &amp;#8640; c \coloneqq \langle f, c_{(2)}\rangle c_{(1)},
          %p or
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mi ⇀
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi g
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle g, f &amp;#8640; c\rangle = \langle f, c_{(2)}\rangle
                  \\langle g, c_{(1)}\rangle = \langle g f, c\rangle
          %p
            According to the suggestion of Nichols, one reads
            = succeed "\u21C0" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            hits
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            = succeed "\u21BC" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is hit by
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %p
            Similarly (cf. Montgomery 1.6.6), if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an algebra and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
            its algebraic dual, one also defines harpoon actions as transposes to left and right multiplications, for example for right multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi h
                  %mi ↼
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle h &amp;#8636; f, k\rangle = \langle f, k h\rangle.
          %p
            Now, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in A^\circ
            is in finite dual, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(f)
            makes sense, hence, in Sweedler notation,
            = succeed "\u21C0" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f=\langle f_{(2)}, h\rangle f_{(1)}
          %p We also define here left and right coadjoint actions and coactions, cf. Majid.
          %p One should also treat rationality: a module is rational if it corresponds to a comodule of the finite dual coalgebra.
          %h2#paired_bialgebras Paired bialgebras
          %p
            For
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigebra"} bigebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
          %p
            Two
            = succeed "-bigebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            are
            %strong paired
            if there is a bilinear map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle,\rangle: B\otimes H\to k
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b\in B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h,g\in H
            the equations
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Δ
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
